00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.280
Cream's voyage diary:

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:41.780
On August 21, the Metarex have attacked Blue Typhoon for 12 hours.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.330
It's a strange and cruel attack.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.260
Metarex spaceships 35 degrees to the right!

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.630
Three are approaching!

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:01.260
Course 135 yellow. Speed 1.3 sols.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.930
Distance: 25,000 space kilometers.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:10.230
26,000... 27,000... 28,000...

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:16.820
30,000... Metarex went to the green area.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.320
I told you they're afraid of us!

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.950
I'm not sure...

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.330
But like before, we don't know when they'll attack.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.790
Stay with Master Emerald, Knuckles!

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.580
I don't want to.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.090
If we're always running away, it doesn't matter where I am.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.050
That's true.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.970
We've been in this situation for 5 hours.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.350
Is this Metarex's goal?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.520
Hey, Tails.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.060
Let's try going off-course.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.360
What do you mean?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.360
Is something going to happen if we stay on this course?

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.650
No, just the opposite.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:03.370
They started attacking us 12 hours ago.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:08.410
We entered this course 5 hours ago to avoid them.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.130
So Metarex wants us to follow this path?

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.590
That's what they want?

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.380
That's what we're going to find out!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:23.850
Okay! I'll test how good their tracking radar is!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.140
Chris, increase the left auxiliary engine's output by 0.5 %!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.060
Roger. Up count at 5 seconds.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.730
That won't change the heading much.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.150
Here they come!

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.730
High energy detected 25 degrees to the right.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.440
Shields on!

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.700
They don't want us heading in that direction.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.790
Port side 10 degrees, output 20%!

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.420
They're coming on course 285.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.920
There are three ships and five more behind them!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.420
Chris, destroy the three ships!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.180
Roger!

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.430
Cut engine output.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.300
Bring us back to course 1109!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:06.760
Okay!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.020
Firing interceptor missiles!

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.440
Three ships destroyed!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.950
We're back to course 1109.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.580
The next five ships are coming, right on course!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.950
Cream, have the shields ready.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:31.700
Roger!

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.580
We'll now find out the truth.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.840
Metarex changed course and are heading for the green area.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.470
No doubt about it, Sonic.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.350
Yeah.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.480
Chris, what's up ahead?

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:58.900
The long-range radar has been offline since entering Metarex space.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.030
This is the best I can do.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.360
It's like a television without an antenna.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.370
Let's keep going straight on this course.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.370
You seem eager to fight. What's up? You have more lines of dialogue than usual.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.120
Are you changing character?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:20.250
My spines are tingling.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:29.070
Episode 67

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:29.070
The Black Trap

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:36.190
It's as if you're sending them an invitation, Black.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.360
It's important to take your time on the fun things in life.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.280
Fun things?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.160
Dark, you're so busy lately that you don't have time to play with me.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.540
No matter which planet I attack, I win in an instant.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.370
I need more excitement.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:03.550
I don't want to repeat myself, but Red Pine didn't underestimate them.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.460
I know.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.800
I won't take them lightly.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:13.390
Because Dark, though I expected it with Red Pine, there's someone who can physically hurt you, right?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:16.230
Don't worry.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.980
The fact that I'm excited proves that I'm concentrating.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:28.700
What I hate the most is regret.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.250
I've detected a planet 50,000 space kilometers ahead.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.590
What? The radar is working now?

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.340
No, it's not fixed.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.920
We're in a position to see it.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.180
You're saying that we're coming near it.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.430
Enlarging the image on the main screen!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.140
It's tiny!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.640
Can't you make it bigger?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.190
It's hard. Maybe if I use the super digital zoom...

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.360
What's that? Octopus tentacles?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.610
That's a lot of craters. They're all over the planet.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.530
Does that mean a lot of meteors hit that planet?

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.660
No!

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.540
It was destroyed!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.290
It was attacked over and over until it turned into that!

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:26.800
Attacked over and over...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.260
Until all life was gone...

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.640
How horrible...

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.980
Cosmo!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:47.650
Tails, I know we have to find the Chaos Emeralds as fast as possible.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:55.370
But will you just let me destroy that?

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:02.710
Even though we don't have time to waste on these Metarex, I'm willing to make an exception!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.170
Yeah, let's get rid of them quickly!

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.710
Engine output 100%! Cutting shield power!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.760
Chaos Emeralds?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.850
Tails, is this...

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.270
Yeah, it's strange.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.770
What's wrong?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:28.610
Tails fixed the system so that it won't detect fakes.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.200
How do you know it's fake? It might be real.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.990
There can't be this many real ones!

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.490
Many? How many?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.080
500!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.700
I think I'm getting a heartburn.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:46.210
They used a crystal to create fake Chaos Emeralds. We have that data in our computers.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.340
That means their forgery skills are improving.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.050
You shouldn't admire them for that!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.130
Look at the main monitor.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.010
It's a message from that planet.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.100
They're sending us an e-mail?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.060
I'll run it through the translation machine.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.390
You don't have to. I can read it.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.060
"Welcome to our universe."

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:10.730
"I respect you for your courage."

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.990
"I will allow you to visit this planet."

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.990
"One of the four Metarex bosses..."

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.330
"Black Narcissus."

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.830
So he's allowing us to visit him!

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.750
He gets on my nerves!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:31.250
Be careful, Knuckles. You always lose your cool in these situations.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.300
You don't get to choose my character traits!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:33.970
Told you so.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.180
There they go again.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.470
"P.S."

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.760
Cosmo, is there something else?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.850
No, that's the whole message.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.770
Really!

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.440
Okay! Let's go visit him!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.480
He might hold a welcome party for us.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.530
Cheese, you really like to eat.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.650
Everyone, I'm sorry.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.670
Missiles from the Metarex base!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.380
What's the meaning of this?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.260
I'm transferring power to the shields!

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.720
He was trying to catch us off-guard!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.810
That sneak never intended to welcome us!

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.020
Cosmo?

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.560
Chris?

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.520
They're coming!

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.570
Shoot them down!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.860
This is strange.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:24.780
They contain potassium and aluminum, so it doesn't make sense.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.240
Can you explain that to me?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.960
In other words, the missiles are actually fireworks.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.550
How stupid! Fireworks to welcome us?

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:30.520
Where are you? I came alone, as promised!

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.480
You don't have to shout.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.980
I can hear you.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.940
You said that you'll tell me everything.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:46.280
What happened between the Cosmo tribe and the Metarex?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.200
I said that you don't need to shout.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.410
Don't you understand your position?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.040
You fool. You're a hostage.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.800
Hostage?

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.600
"To the survivor of the Cosmo tribe..."

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:20.860
"If you want to learn the truth, the bright missile in 5 minutes will give you your opportunity."

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.780
I'm giving you minus points, Captain! This is why we have a translation machine!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.030
You're right.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.370
Don't be so hard on him.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.660
We should focus on finding Cosmo as fast as we can.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:36.250
Yeah, she's definitely somewhere on the Blue Typhoon.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.500
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.920
Amy's ship is gone.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.050
What?

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:45.590
No way! How could she leave without triggering the bridge's sensors?

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.140
It seems we have a professional hacker.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.760
The only one who can do this is Chris!

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.810
Yeah...

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:00.730
If you're willing to talk and work things out...

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:01.690
Stop!

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.990
I didn't invite you, so how dare you speak up.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.740
I'm not interested in you at all. Leave.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:13.120
I'm sorry, Chris.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:15.080
I understand, Cosmo.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.370
I also did the same things when I was young.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:24.050
But since you said you're our friend, don't do this again.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.800
Right! I am your friend!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.510
That's why...

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.800
You're making me blush, Cosmo.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.560
I feel like I'm looking at myself from 6 years ago.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.890
You, Chris?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:39.400
I'll tell you when we get back to the Blue Typhoon.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.020
But don't tease me.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.270
What are you thinking?

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.320
I can't let her leave.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.240
That's what I expected!

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:50.490
Let's go, Cosmo!

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.410
I'm about to lose my temper.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.590
Leave it to me. I'm used to these situations.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.430
Let's go, Cosmo!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.150
Chris!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:32.570
Wild animals need to be trained to behave.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:38.040
I haven't felt this excited in a long time.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:52.470
Amy and Cream, we can't use the laser gun. Use the Vulcan and missiles instead.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:57.810
Sheesh, even Chris? Why can't men learn to work in groups?

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:01.520
I know. We already have our hands full with Knuckles!

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:04.690
If you're gonna talk behind my back, then turn off the microphone!

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.440
Oops, I forgot.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.730
Liar!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.240
Tails, I can turn it up to 100%, right?

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:14.570
Yes. Since they're facing one of the four Metarex bosses, we need to go directly to the central chamber.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.330
Is that okay with you, Sonic?

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:21.080
Sure! I'll hurry up and give him a lecture.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.590
You take care of Chris. I'll give Cosmo a piece of my mind.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.090
Unlocking the chamber!

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:31.550
That's right. She shouldn't have left without telling us!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.390
What's he saying, Cream?

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.850
He says that he'll lecture her.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:41.060
Here we go! Connecting energy to the hammer!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:46.230
Pressurizing the cannon rod's ring energy!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:51.690
Sonic, start your spin!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.570
Trigger safety off!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.870
Targeting Metarex base straight ahead!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.790
Fire Sonic Driver!

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.480
What's going on?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.810
They made so many fakes.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.440
Their glow is eerie.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.440
How long do you plan to stay there?

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.200
I'm over here.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.660
Come up here.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.460
I've been waiting for you.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.250
Sonic, the one who controls the light of chaos.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:56.590
I'm sorry that I broke your base. I didn't know where the entrance was.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.550
And I had more urgent business.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.350
No problem.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:07.520
Besides, I wanted to see if the Sonic Driver's power matched our data. I'm surprised.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.690
According to our calculations, you were supposed to stop in this room.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.940
However...

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:16.900
Sorry, but everyone's waiting for me to come home.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.030
Give me back my two friends.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:22.660
Don't be so cold.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:27.040
I need you to show me if your strength matches our data.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.290
You really love data, don't you?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.420
Who cares about data?

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.010
You'll indulge me, won't you?

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.970
Don't worry. They're not dead.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.020
Chris!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.520
Cosmo!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.280
Don't try to break the glass.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:59.740
The two trapped inside will disintegrate in an instant.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.700
If you don't do as I wish...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.250
Well, you already know what will happen.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:13.630
Cosmo's cheeks were swollen...

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.510
So?

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.840
What did you do to Chris?

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:26.520
Punishment is required to make animals behave.

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.100
Sonic, there are my proud creations.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:40.030
Gold and Silver. Gold will test your power, while Silver will test your speed.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:45.870
If your abilities match our data, it should be a good battle.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:51.120
You really want me to fight?

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.720
Is this what you wanted to see?

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.760
That's enough!

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.890
Stop already, Sonic.

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.400
They're totally destroyed!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.520
We can't use them.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:20.320
Sorry, the Egg Drive had a miscalculation.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:25.410
We don't have much time left, so let's end this.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:27.580
Sonic...

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.160
Don't disappoint me.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:35.630
You can't allow anger and hatred to overwhelm you.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:40.090
I'll pretend that I didn't see anything. Go disappear into the smoke.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:45.760
Don't worry about the other two. I'm sure he's already taken care of the situation.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.310
That was reckless of you.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:54.230
I've now paid you back for the limiters.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:58.230
Screw Kick!

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.150
She lost her temper.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.200
She's also upset.

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.120
Stop doing this!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:12.460
I'll make you pay if you build something this troubling again!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.920
Handle the rest, Doctor.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:16.960
Leave it to me.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.500
Thanks for your help!

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:21.630
That's all I have for this episode? Call the producer!

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.800
Look what you've done!

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.930
You made too many mistakes.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:33.230
We also take hostages, but we don't hurt them.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.890
That's not cool!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:38.110
You shouldn't build things like that either.

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:40.110
It's illegal!

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.280
Furthermore...

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:42.030
Shut up!

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:44.360
I don't think so!

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.910
What?

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:48.990
Bokkun Kick!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.330
Don't underestimate us, idiot!

00:21:55.620 --> 00:22:01.420
You made another mistake. They're also my bodyguards.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.970
Huh? We're "also" bodyguards? Then what are we usually?

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:05.470
Comedy robots.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:06.630
No way!

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:08.850
Of course you are!

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:10.600
I'll make you cry if you keep talking like that!

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:11.890
So arrogant!

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:14.390
That's enough. Let's go home.

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:17.060
Sorry to bother you, Black something.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:20.440
I'm sure we'll meet again soon.

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:30.200
I think they now realize that this battle is about to enter a new phase.

